# Frontend Rules

## Stack
- UI = HTL (Sightly) for markup + TypeScript for logic, built via the ui.frontend
  Webpack pipeline into AEM clientlibs
- TypeScript is the DEFAULT/standard for new code
- Plain JavaScript (.js) is PERMITTED where it is simpler; Webpack/ts-loader allows
  .js alongside .ts (entry: ui.frontend/src/main/webpack). Do not force-convert trivial JS to TS.

## Where Code Lives
- TypeScript/JS source: ui.frontend/src/main/webpack (site/, components/)
- Compiled output → AEM clientlibs (do NOT hand-edit generated clientlibs)
- HTL components: /apps/assessment/components
- Clientlib category namespace: assessment.ticketing

## TypeScript Standards (apply to .ts files)
- Use ES modules (import/export), async/await for fetch
- Prefer explicit types for function params, return values, and API DTOs
- Define interfaces for API payloads (e.g., Ticket, Comment, User) mirroring backend DTOs
- Enable/respect tsconfig strictness already generated by the archetype
- No `any` unless justified with a comment
- Keep functions small and pure where possible

## JavaScript (when used)
- Same module style (import/export), async/await
- Add lightweight JSDoc for shared functions
- Do not introduce a second bundler or framework

## API & Behavior Rules (both TS and JS)
- Talk ONLY to REST endpoints under /bin/api/v1/* (never JCR/GraphQL directly)
- Always handle loading, empty, and error states from fetch()
- Escape/encode any user-provided content rendered into the DOM (prevent XSS)
- Status dropdown must offer ONLY valid next transitions for the ticket's current status
- No hardcoded hostnames or secrets — use relative /bin/api/v1 paths

## Components (small, reusable)
- ticket-list, ticket-card, ticket-form, ticket-detail, comment-list, status-badge

## Build
- Use the archetype's npm/webpack scripts (package.json in ui.frontend)
- Vanilla JS test files are acceptable (as you confirmed .js works within main.ts entry)
